.TH LIBMU2E_SENDER 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-dataformat-viewer t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
libmu2e_sender, mu2e_send, mu2e_send_tcp, mu2e_send_udp, mu2e_strerror \- send raw bytes over TCP or UDP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqmu2e_sender.h\(dq
.PP
.BI "int mu2e_send(mu2e_protocol_t " proto ", const char *" host ", int " port ,
.BI "              const uint8_t *" data ", size_t " len );
.BI "int mu2e_send_tcp(const char *" host ", int " port ", const uint8_t *" data ", size_t " len );
.BI "int mu2e_send_udp(const char *" host ", int " port ", const uint8_t *" data ", size_t " len );
.B const char *mu2e_strerror(void);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.BR \-lmu2e_sender .
.SH DESCRIPTION
A C-linkage library (implemented in C++17) built by
.IR cpp/CMakeLists.txt
as target
.B mu2e_sender
(static unless
.B BUILD_SHARED_LIBS
is set; SOVERSION 1).
.PP
.B mu2e_send()
resolves
.I host
with
.BR getaddrinfo (3)
(IPv4 or IPv6).
For
.B MU2E_PROTO_TCP
it connects to the first address that accepts, sends all
.I len
bytes (looping on partial writes) and closes.
For
.B MU2E_PROTO_UDP
it sends one datagram to the first address.
A new socket is used per call.
.B mu2e_send_tcp()
and
.B mu2e_send_udp()
are wrappers.
.PP
.B mu2e_strerror()
returns a thread-local message describing the last failure.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success, \-1 on failure.
.SH ERRORS
On a
.B getaddrinfo
failure the message is set but
.I errno
is not.
.B send
uses no
.BR MSG_NOSIGNAL ,
so a peer that has closed the connection raises SIGPIPE in the caller.
The library uses POSIX sockets only and does not build on Windows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include "mu2e_sender.h"
uint8_t pkt[16] = {0x00,0x10,0x80,0x10};
if (mu2e_send_tcp("localhost", 7755, pkt, sizeof pkt) != 0)
    fprintf(stderr, "%s\en", mu2e_strerror());
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I cpp/include/mu2e_sender.h
.TP
.I cpp/src/mu2e_sender.cpp
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2e_send (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
